  "_source": "Stage 7 (Claude Code, 08.10): the shape of lexicon §5.22 „menus.json”. One menu `eindejaar-2026`, opened in the bestelbon by `?menu=` + its `param`; `deadline` ISO date or null → [DATUM]; `pickup` = the two days the plan assumes (24 and 31 December, build plan row 7 — B 3 / B 11 confirm them), `from`/`to` null → [UUR] and the day's opening hours in the bestelbon; `items` = the board's seven stand-in rows (§5.22 table), `price` null → [PRIJS] (Gourmet 9's €10 on the board is the old site's price, FACTS — not used), `unit` kg | pers | stuk (gourmet 9 and luxe: min 2 persons, as gourmet-9 in products.json); `message` = lexicon §5.10 eindejaar without its dots — the bestelbon puts the order after it (§5.22 „the bestelbon fills the dots”); `pickupOnly` = the line the bestelbon shows when a menu row is chosen (menu orders are pickup only — §5.22 „Answers to Claude Code's stage-7 report”, 08.10 17:50; RO kept for stage 9); `mail` = the menu's word in the shop's mail (subject NL „Bestelling {REF} · Eindejaarsmenu · afhalen …”, first line RO „… · meniul de sărbători · ridicare …”, same source). The rows have the products.json shape so the bestelbon lists them under „Eindejaarsmenu 2026” (/bestellen?menu=eindejaar). The owners' folder replaces the rows wholesale (B 11); Cowork fills this file at stage 15. Row 15a (Claude Code, 13.10): the owners' folder is in — `sections` = the brochure's eight sections in its order (docs/data/price-list.json `menu_eindejaar.section_order`, names NL / RO from that file; the vleeshoofdgerechten carry the note „per portie van 200 g” / „porție de 200 g” on their section, not on each row); `items` = its 51 rows, ids `ej26-` + the products.json id, each with its `section`, name, line (persons, contents), price and unit as in products.json ([OWNER] 13.10, FACTS); the seven stand-in rows are gone. `deadline` and the pickup hours stay null → [DATUM] / [UUR] (B 11 / B 3).",
